<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia FACB in chemical foam venture.</title>
<headline>Malaysia FACB in chemical foam venture.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>FACB Bhd said on Friday it has entered into a joint venture agreement with HT Troplast AG of Germany to set up a 20 million ringgit plant to make advanced grades of chemical crosslinked polyethylene foam.</p>
<p>In a statement, FACB said the venture will be done through Facell Foam Sdn Bhd in which FACB and HT Troplast AG will each hold equal stakes of 50 percent.</p>
<p>The plant to be located in Malaysia will have an initial production capacity of 1,000 metric tonnes a year, it said.</p>
<p>The foam is used in various applications including automotive, air-conditioning, insulation and packaging.</p>
<p>FACB said it expects the venture to contribute positively to future earnings.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603 201 4813)</p>
</text>
